    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0038" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg24"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (3)A/9–944: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Reed</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos Aires</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-09">September 9,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received September 9—7:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2346. The Argentine Foreign Office has just issued a communiqué stating that
                    “under the circumstances and much against its wishes” it has instructed the
                    Argentine representative to the Political Defense Committee in Montevideo to
                    inform the Committee that “the Argentine Republic has been placed in a position
                    of having to withdraw from said organization.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reed</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
